<section class="section section--flush page-hero"><div class="container prose"><h1>References and Projects</h1></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><p>ISYSTEMS AUTOMATION has delivered control, protection and optimization systems since 2007. The list below covers projects carried out by the company. Where a client requires confidentiality, the site is described by type rather than by name.</p>
<dl><div><dt>Since 2007</dt><dd>Company founded in Ploiești, Romania</dd></div><div><dt>ISO 9001</dt><dd>Certified since 2009</dd></div><div><dt>260 t/h at 100 bar</dt><dd>Largest CFB boiler under our control system</dd></div><div><dt>6 DCS platforms</dt><dd>Ovation, ABB 800xA, ABB Symphony, PCS7, TIA Portal, Centum VP</dd></div><div><dt>SIL 2 / SIL 3</dt><dd>Safety applications certified to IEC 61511</dd></div><div><dt>4 countries</dt><dd>Romania, Serbia, Kazakhstan, Russia</dd></div></dl>
<h2 class="section-title">What we do on site</h2>
<h4>Engineering and design</h4>
<ul>
<li>DCS conceptual architecture, I/O databases, control logic and control narratives, HMI design and alarm schemes</li>
<li>ESD and Burner Management System architecture, test and FAT procedures</li>
<li>SIL 2 and SIL 3 certification support to IEC 61511</li>
<li>I&amp;C design verification against local and international standards</li>
<li>P&amp;ID, cable schedules, panel design, hook-up and as-built documentation</li>
<li>Procurement of control and instrumentation equipment</li>
</ul>
<h4>Commissioning and operation</h4>
<ul>
<li>Factory and site acceptance testing, loop checks, functional testing, loop tuning</li>
<li>Autonomous plant operation with remote control over four redundant IEC 60870-5-104 channels</li>
<li>Turbine acceptance testing: quality of primary and secondary frequency regulation, rate of load change, generator disconnection from the grid, emergency stops</li>
<li>Boiler efficiency by direct and indirect method for gas and petroleum coke fired CFB boilers; steam turbine efficiency and losses; thermal and electrical energy balances</li>
<li>Process data collection from control systems and commercial metering, long-term archiving and calculation</li>
<li>DCS backup, lifecycle updates, and protection of control system assets against internal and external cyber threats</li>
<li>Operator training on new control schemes</li>
</ul>
